@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@tenantId = REPLACE_WITH_BOOTSTRAP_TENANT_ID
@organizationId = REPLACE_WITH_ORGANIZATION_UUID
@integrationId = REPLACE_WITH_INTEGRATION_UUID
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOGIN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@jobId = REPLACE_WITH_JOB_ID
@candidateId = REPLACE_WITH_CANDIDATE_ID
@applicationId = REPLACE_WITH_APPLICATION_ID
@offerId = REPLACE_WITH_OFFER_ID
@employeeId = REPLACE_WITH_EMPLOYEE_ID
@leaveRequestId = REPLACE_WITH_LEAVE_REQUEST_ID
@interviewId = REPLACE_WITH_INTERVIEW_ID
@panelistUserId = REPLACE_WITH_ACTIVE_PANELIST_USER_ID
@panelistToken = REPLACE_WITH_PANELIST_LOGIN_TOKEN

### Login: use the email/password configured for bootstrap.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}",
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD"
}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a requisition
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Senior Node.js Developer",
  "description": "Build and maintain TypeScript services with PostgreSQL.",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "location": "Bengaluru",
  "screeningCriteria": [{"id":"nodejs","label":"Node.js","weight":100,"must_have":true}]
}

### Approve job
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Publish to the internal listing only
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create candidate; email is deduplicated within the tenant.
POST {{baseUrl}}/candidates
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Sample Candidate",
  "email": "candidate@example.com",
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

### Create application
POST {{baseUrl}}/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jobId": "{{jobId}}",
  "candidateId": "{{candidateId}}"
}

### Human shortlisting
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage": "SHORTLISTED"
}

### Record call consent with an evidence reference; other scopes are independent.
POST {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scope": "CALL",
  "granted": true,
  "source": "Candidate consent form reference CONSENT-001"
}

### AI call: needs CALL_PLANNING_ENABLED=true, AI calling on, Plivo and a voice AI
### (docs/ai-calling.md). Outside calling hours it waits for the next window.
POST {{baseUrl}}/call-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}",
  "language": "EN",
  "recording": false,
  "transcription": false,
  "idempotencyKey": "sample-call-plan-001"
}

### Draft offer: monetary value is a decimal string.
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}",
  "annualCtc": "1800000.00",
  "currency": "INR",
  "joiningDate": "2027-01-11"
}

### Approve offer
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### HR records acceptance evidence; no candidate portal/e-signature exists yet.
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "acceptanceReference": "Candidate acceptance email stored under OFFER-001"
}

### Hire: retrying this same offer returns its existing employee.
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/hire
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Paginated staff lists
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Initial onboarding tasks created by hire-to-join
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}/onboarding-tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### HR records a leave request; leave balances/accruals are future work.
POST {{baseUrl}}/leave-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "{{employeeId}}",
  "type": "ANNUAL",
  "startDate": "2027-01-18",
  "endDate": "2027-01-19",
  "reason": "Personal leave"
}

### HR reviews a pending leave request
POST {{baseUrl}}/leave-requests/{{leaveRequestId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "APPROVED"
}

### HR records one attendance entry per employee/work date
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendance
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": "{{employeeId}}",
  "workDate": "2027-01-12",
  "checkIn": "2027-01-12T09:00:00+05:30",
  "checkOut": "2027-01-12T18:00:00+05:30"
}

### Revoke calling consent; affected pending plans are cancelled.
POST {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scope": "CALL",
  "granted": false,
  "source": "Candidate opt-out email reference OPTOUT-001"
}


### Milestone A: extended job requirements (use existing token variables)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Backend Engineer","description":"Build secure tenant APIs","department":"Engineering","location":"Remote","openings":2,"employmentType":"FULL_TIME","salaryMin":1000000,"salaryMax":1500000,"screeningCriteria":[{"id":"typescript","label":"TypeScript experience","weight":25,"must_have":true}]}

### Assign an active hiring manager (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId":"REPLACE_WITH_MANAGER_UUID","role":"HIRING_MANAGER"}

### List/revoke assignments
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Revoke
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/assignments/REPLACE_WITH_ASSIGNMENT_UUID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Human rejection with required reason
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/stage
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"stage":"REJECTED","reasonCode":"EXPERIENCE","note":"Reviewed by the hiring manager"}

### Immutable stage history
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search and paginate; response also includes total
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications?jobId={{jobId}}&stage=SHORTLISTED&q=example&sort=created_at&direction=desc&limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Close a job
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"closeReason":"Position filled"}

### Revised offer: close the prior pending offer first, then POST /offers again
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### New revision with optional expiry
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"applicationId":"{{applicationId}}","annualCtc":"1500000.00","currency":"INR","joiningDate":"2027-01-01","expiresAt":"2099-01-01T00:00:00Z"}

### Record decline / expire a due pending offer (admin only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/decline
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Expire (409 before expiresAt)
POST {{baseUrl}}/offers/{{offerId}}/expire
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Milestone B: configure a public slug through bootstrap, or use tenant-<UUID>
@tenantSlug = tenant-REPLACE_WITH_TENANT_UUID
@documentId = REPLACE_WITH_DOCUMENT_UUID

### Public published jobs and current noticeVersion (no authentication)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/{{tenantSlug}}/jobs?limit=25&offset=0

### Public job details (no staff-only fields)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/{{tenantSlug}}/jobs/{{jobId}}

### Public intake: all three consents are independent and default false
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/{{tenantSlug}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName":"Example Applicant","email":"applicant@example.test","phone":"+919876543210","noticeVersion":"2026-11-v1","consents":{"CALL":false,"RECORDING":false,"TRANSCRIPTION":false},"website":""}

### Optional public resume: add {"resume":{"filename":"resume.pdf","base64":"<BASE64>"}} to intake (max 512 KiB)
### New/existing/duplicate submissions return the same 202 message; consent remains unverified.

### Staff multipart upload; replace ./resume.pdf with a real local PDF/DOCX
POST {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=resume-boundary

--resume-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./resume.pdf
--resume-boundary--

### Staff document metadata (private object keys are never returned)
GET {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audited attachment download: returns 409 until a real scanner returns CLEAN
GET {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/documents/{{documentId}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin erasure: documentsPending=0 confirms object deletion; retry if positive
POST {{baseUrl}}/candidates/{{candidateId}}/erase
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### CLI: npm run build
### CLI preview: npm run retention -- --tenant-id <UUID> --actor-id <ADMIN_UUID> --dry-run
### CLI execute: npm run retention -- --tenant-id <UUID> --actor-id <ADMIN_UUID> --limit 100

### Milestone C: schedule locally (staff); use future dates and a SHORTLISTED/INTERVIEW application.
### VIDEO requires a manually supplied HTTPS link. No calendar event or meeting link is generated.
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}",
  "round": "Technical 1",
  "mode": "VIDEO",
  "startsAt": "2027-01-15T10:00:00+05:30",
  "endsAt": "2027-01-15T11:00:00+05:30",
  "meetingUrl": "https://meet.example.com/manual-interview-link",
  "panelistIds": ["{{panelistUserId}}"]
}

### Staff see tenant interviews; HM/interviewer users see only actual panel membership.
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews?applicationId={{applicationId}}&limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Detail includes frozen criteria_snapshot and panelist_ids.
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{interviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reschedule both timestamps together; conflicting panelist reservations return 409.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{interviewId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startsAt": "2027-01-15T11:00:00+05:30",
  "endsAt": "2027-01-15T12:00:00+05:30"
}

### Submit once using the actual panelist's token; match ALL frozen criterion IDs.
### scores: [] is valid only when criteria_snapshot is empty. Submission never changes hiring stage.
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{interviewId}}/scorecards
Authorization: Bearer {{panelistToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "scores": [{"criterionId":"nodejs","score":4}],
  "recommendation": "HIRE",
  "notes": "Evidence-based technical assessment"
}

### Staff read all cards for this interview; HM/interviewers read only their own submissions.
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{interviewId}}/scorecards
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Staff cancellation is idempotent and releases active panelist reservations.
POST {{baseUrl}}/interviews/{{interviewId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason":"Candidate requested cancellation"}

### Reports: only recruiter/admin roles, strict query, inclusive from/exclusive to, maximum 366 days.
### Use observed historical periods; omit dates for the last 30 days. Durations are seconds.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/recruitment/funnel?jobId={{jobId}}&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dwell: clipped positive visits; terminal HIRED/REJECTED dwell excluded.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/recruitment/time-in-stage?jobId={{jobId}}&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Time to hire excludes and counts missing APPLIED/reversed evidence; no fabricated zero duration.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/recruitment/time-to-hire?jobId={{jobId}}&from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Verify the single-use token from the development email log
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/{{tenantSlug}}/contact-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"<selector>.<secret>"}

### Milestone E: deployed readiness (production /docs is blocked)
# Replace the domain; never put a verification token in a URL query.
GET https://careers.your-domain.test/api/v1/health/ready

### Verification client reads tenant/token from the email link fragment and POSTs here.
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/{{tenantSlug}}/contact-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"{{verificationToken}}"}

### Browser session (same-origin only; HttpOnly cookie issued, no token body)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/session
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Content-Type: application/json

{"tenantId":"{{tenantId}}","email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Browser who-am-I and expiration
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/session

### Browser logout (clears cookie)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/auth/session
Origin: http://localhost:5173

### SaaS platform sign-in (organization key, no build-time tenant UUID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizationSlug":"platform","email":"owner@example.test","password":"SET_LOCALLY_DO_NOT_COMMIT"}

### Platform Super Admin: create organization and email its initial admin invite
POST {{baseUrl}}/saas/organizations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Example Company","slug":"example-company","adminName":"Organization Admin","adminEmail":"admin@example.test"}

### Organization Admin: invite staff (cannot select platform/admin roles)
POST {{baseUrl}}/saas/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"fullName":"Hiring Manager","email":"manager@example.test","role":"HIRING_MANAGER"}

### Recipient: accept the latest invitation; no role or user ID in this body
POST {{baseUrl}}/saas/invitations/accept
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizationSlug":"example-company","token":"PASTE_ONE_TIME_TOKEN_LOCALLY","password":"CHOOSE_12_TO_128_CHARACTERS"}

### Organization Admin: current-organization team (pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/saas/users?limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter platform audit evidence, including integration overrides for an organization
GET {{baseUrl}}/super-admin/audit-logs?organization_id={{organizationId}}&limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### CSV exports the same filtered page (read-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/super-admin/audit-logs/export?organization_id={{organizationId}}&limit=25&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Resume screening: newest result for an application (or null)
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/screening
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Screen an application's resume now (returns the result or the failure)
POST {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/screening
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Screening progress for a job
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/screening
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Queue screening for a job's unscreened or failed applications
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/screening
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Best matches first, screened only
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications?jobId={{jobId}}&sort=score&screening=screened
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### HR Admin: which AI screens resumes
GET {{baseUrl}}/organization/ai-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### HR Admin: turn on AI calling with Gemini Live (null = automatic)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/organization/ai-settings/calling
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled":true,"provider":"google_ai"}

### The name the AI introduces itself with on calls (null: none)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/organization/ai-settings/calling
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"enabled":true,"assistantName":"Priya"}

### The Candidates page: shortlisted onward, with each stage's count
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications?stages=SHORTLISTED,INTERVIEW,OFFER,HIRED&counts=true&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Who can sit on an interview panel
GET {{baseUrl}}/interviews/panelists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### An application's calls: whether it can be called, consents, answers
GET {{baseUrl}}/applications/{{applicationId}}/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Call every shortlisted candidate of a job who agreed to be called
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{jobId}}/calls
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"language":"EN","recording":true,"transcription":true}

### Cancel a waiting call, or hang up one on the line
POST {{baseUrl}}/call-requests/{{callRequestId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A browser test call: returns a one-time ticket for /api/v1/calls/test/:ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/calls/test-sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"jobId":"{{jobId}}","language":"EN"}

### Draft a job's AI call questions for review (not saved)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/call-questions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Senior PHP Developer","department":"Engineering","location":"Noida","description":"Build and maintain Laravel services. Night shifts twice a month.","screeningCriteria":[{"id":"c1","label":"4+ years of Laravel","must_have":true}]}

### HR Admin: screen with Anthropic only (null = automatic order)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/organization/ai-settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"screeningProvider":"anthropic","screeningFallback":false}

### A failed sandbox test revokes corresponding production approval
POST {{baseUrl}}/super-admin/integrations/{{integrationId}}/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
